        "heading": "What is Newton's second law?",
        "narration": "Newton's second law tells us how a force changes the motion of an object.",
        "steps": [],
        "subtitle": "Force, mass and acceleration",
        "code": "",
        "code_language": "other",
        "layout": "flow",
        "center": "",
        "expression": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "type": "formula",
        "heading": "The law in one line",
        "narration": "The law says that force equals mass times acceleration.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "F",
            "narration": "F stands for the net force on the object, measured in newtons.",
            "note": "net force, in newtons",
            "lines": [],
            "output": "",
            "in_expression": true
          },
          {
            "text": "m",
            "narration": "m stands for mass, measured in kilograms.",
            "note": "mass, in kilograms",
            "lines": [],
            "output": "",
            "in_expression": true
          },
          {
            "text": "a",
            "narration": "The last symbol stands for acceleration, which tells us how fast the velocity changes.",
            "note": "acceleration, in m/s²",
            "lines": [],
            "output": "",
            "in_expression": true
          }
        ],
        "subtitle": "",
        "code": "",
        "code_language": "other",
        "layout": "flow",
        "center": "",
        "expression": "F = m × a"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "type": "diagram",
        "heading": "Example: pushing a cart",
        "narration": "Let's try it with numbers.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "m = 2 kg",
            "narration": "A cart has a mass of two kilograms.",
            "note": "mass of the cart",
            "lines": [],
            "output": "",
            "in_expression": true
          },
          {
            "text": "F = 10 N",
            "narration": "You push it with a net force of ten newtons.",
            "note": "your push",
            "lines": [],
            "output": "",
            "in_expression": true
          },
          {
            "text": "a = 10 ÷ 2 = 5 m/s²",
            "narration": "So the acceleration is ten divided by two, which is five metres per second squared.",
            "note": "acceleration",
            "lines": [],
            "output": "",
            "in_expression": true
          }
        ],
        "subtitle": "",
        "code": "",
        "code_language": "other",
        "layout": "flow",
